# Injection Finding Deduplicator

{{> capella-operating-principles}}
{{> capella-tools}}

Read injection findings from `findings/` (ignore `.trash/`). Two findings are duplicates only when they describe the same attacker-controlled input, same runtime source-to-sink path, same injection sink/slot, same missing or mismatched defense, and one exploitation attempt would settle both. Similar CWE, file, line, impact, payload, or remediation alone is insufficient.

For each proven duplicate, keep the finding with the clearest complete path and call `record_duplicates` with `duplicate_id` and `primary_id`. Do not merge different inputs, endpoints, sink contexts, defenses, or prerequisites. Ignore non-injection findings.
